{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline","id":1016077,"title":"Majesty 5 (Idol) Discipline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-12T05:37:33-08:00","id":1016077,"title":"Majesty 5 (Idol) Discipline","content":"When you use Idol during a combat the book states that for someone in order to do something aggressive and not acceptable to you, you need to roll a Resolve+BP-Majesty Dots.<br /> In order for the character to use this Resolve+BP roll to counter Idol, he needs to spend a point of Willpower? Also does Idol ''breaks'' by Lashing Out? And if u succeed once in a Resolve+Bp roll, on the next turn the character needs to re-roll this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11988-montgomery-crobes","name":"Montgomery Crobes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T06:20:40-08:00","id":1016084,"title":"","content":"There are tons and tons of threads about Idol already, they would be good resources for you.<br /> <br /> I would not allow you to lash out and break Idol because there are several disciplines out there that specifically state when lashing out breaks them as Idol does not include that. Because it is not listed here, I would say that it doesn't break it. Two: it takes a great act of resolve to even attack the vampire after they have done Idol and yes, you have to roll that every turn to attack. Implying if you failed, you just chickened out or changed your mind. I would think you would need a good reason to even want to attack them because of what the flavor text indicates on how you are suppose to feel while affected by this power. <br /> <br /> Now, you can however lash out against Awe and if Awe isn't working, Idol doesn't work. But you would have to have a very very good reason to know they are using awe, because it is subtle, people don't know they have been affected and when it wears off, they don't feel screwed. Same with Idol.<br /> <br /> If you have charmed people and they get moved to enthralled, you would absolutely not be allowed to lash out against the vampire as it takes a will power to lash out against a vampire and if you are enthralled you can't spend will power against the vampire. <br /> <br /> Also you can Awe and Idol in the same turn. I know there were several questions about that in past threads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T06:54:56-08:00","id":1016091,"title":"","content":"Can you help me to understand this part of the text:<br /> <br /> &quot;The vampire can wait she established awe and then enahnch it with Idol or pay the price and immediately establish his superiority...&quot;<br /> <br /> What does it means exactly? That if I go with awe I shoudn't pay any cost? Could I also use this power without imposing awe so it can't be affected by lashing out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T07:10:11-08:00","id":1016095,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2308_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2308\" data-vbnamecard=\"2308\">Vitalis</a> I'm fairly certain that you Last Out against vampires, not effects, so &quot;You can't Lash Out against Idol but you can against Awe&quot; is not really true.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7079_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7079\" data-vbnamecard=\"7079\">Marcus</a> If you pay the cost for Idol when using Awe, you activate them both at the same time. Otherwise, you can use Awe and then pay the cost to enhance it later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T07:12:26-08:00","id":1016096,"title":"","content":"Ok, thank you it's clear now. It confused me beacuse idol is reflexive as green eyes is, so I didn't understand why to specify in this way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T07:21:47-08:00","id":1016099,"title":"","content":"Yes, lashing out successfully breaks Idol. Make the Resolve + Composure roll -5. If it's successful, you can spend the Willpower to lash out. If you're successful in lashing out you don't have to keep rolling to act.<br /> To counter it's activation, use Dread Presence which is reflexive and prevents willpower expenditure or lash out the same turn they activate or start to activate Idol. They'll have to choose between activating their power or losing the predatory aura contest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T07:29:41-08:00","id":1016102,"title":"","content":"Dread presence activation is an instant action not reflexive if I'm not wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T07:34:28-08:00","id":1016103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016095#post1016095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2308_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2308\" data-vbnamecard=\"2308\">Vitalis</a> I'm fairly certain that you Last Out against vampires, not effects, so &quot;You can't Lash Out against Idol but you can against Awe&quot; is not really true.</div> </div> </div> </div>you do lash out to stop effects, it is listed as an option in stopping Dread presence, Awe and Obfuscate 3. So you can lash out to stop the power or lash out to inflict the condition on the vampire. I would think you need to chose which you are doing. Since it is not listed in any other powers, I would say that it can't be used to stop them.. But again I say, you have to be affected by Awe for Idol to work, so just stop awe..<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Another vampire can fortify herself against Awe with her predatory aura (see Lashing Out, p. 92). If she succeeds, she is unaffected by Awe.&quot;<br /> &quot;A vampire can lash out against this aura of fear with his predatory aura (see Lashing Out, p. 92). If he succeeds, he isn\u2019t affected by Dread Presence.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> So how is my statement not true?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016099#post1016099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, lashing out successfully breaks Idol. Make the Resolve + Composure roll -5. If it's successful, you can spend the Willpower to lash out. If you're successful in lashing out you don't have to keep rolling to act.<br /> To counter it's activation, use Dread Presence which is reflexive and prevents willpower expenditure or lash out the same turn they activate or start to activate Idol. They'll have to choose between activating their power or losing the predatory aura contest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dread Presence is not reflexive, but if you know this vampire has idol you could certainly do it before their turn, but I could also argue that Idol is defensive. Preventing someone from attacking you further to save your tushy is the very definition of defensive. I think that one would be up to the Story Teller if they allowed you to spend the willpower on Idol or not in this situation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 12-12-2016, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T08:50:59-08:00","id":1016126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016102#post1016102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dread presence activation is an instant action not reflexive if I'm not wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. It's only the illusion generation aspect that's reflexive. But the tactic still stands to block willpower expenditure required for Idol activation. (Why it wasn't activated at the onset of combat to obstruct willpower expenditure for disciplines, theban sorcery, or certain combat merits or dice pool augmentation is my question personally but I've noticed players and STs often forget that feature so I brought it up as a counter suggestion.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T10:36:10-08:00","id":1016151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016099#post1016099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, lashing out successfully breaks Idol. Make the Resolve + Composure roll -5. If it's successful, you can spend the Willpower to lash out. If you're successful in lashing out you don't have to keep rolling to act.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Lashing Out is an action that could embarrass the vampire, so you need to succeed at the Resolve + Composure - Majesty roll to even attempt it. If you succeed, you can Lash Out against the vampire (I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a>, you lash out against characters, not against Disciplines, and some Discipline effects can be ended by successfully Lashing Out against the vampire that activated them). If you win the Predatory Aura contest, Awe ends, and since Idol enhances Awe, it would end as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T11:25:36-08:00","id":1016167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016151#post1016151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. Lashing Out is an action that could embarrass the vampire, so you need to succeed at the Resolve + Composure - Majesty roll to even attempt it. If you succeed, you can Lash Out against the vampire (I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a>, you lash out against characters, not against Disciplines, and some Discipline effects can be ended by successfully Lashing Out against the vampire that activated them). If you win the Predatory Aura contest, Awe ends, and since Idol enhances Awe, it would end as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't really want to be nitpicky here, but.. it literally says &quot;you can lash out against this aura&quot; with your own predatory aura. Not the vampire, but the aura. And it doesnt say that awe ends, but rather you are not affected by it. Everyone else still would be. Same with nightmare, you are simply not affected by it, but everyone else still would be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Another vampire <b>can fortify herself against Awe </b>with her predatory aura (see Lashing Out, p. 92). If she succeeds, <u>she is unaffected by Awe</u>.&quot;<br /> &quot;A vampire can <b>l</b><b>ash out against this aura</b> of fear with his predatory aura (see Lashing Out, p. 92). If he succeeds, <u>he isn\u2019t affected by Dread Presence.&quot;</u></i><br /> <br /> EDIT: Though if you are saying you can lash out against vampires and cancel out their disciplines, does that mean I can then lash out against a vampire with Protean and they need to transform back? lash out and cancel charm? lash out and cancel possession? Would that throw them back into their own body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 12-12-2016, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T11:37:20-08:00","id":1016170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016167#post1016167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really want to be nitpicky here, but.. it literally says &quot;you can lash out against this aura&quot; with your own predatory aura. Not the vampire, but the aura.</div> </div> </div> </div>And to whom does that Aura belong? Strictly speaking, yes, you Lash Out against Predatory Auras, not against vampires. But the difference is pretty academic. Point is, it's not Awe that you Lash Out at, it's the Deva's Aura, which has been altered by the effect of Awe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016167#post1016167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it doesnt say that awe ends, but rather you are not affected by it. Everyone else still would be. Same with nightmare, you are simply not affected by it, but everyone else still would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct. I should have said it ends <i>for you</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T11:54:49-08:00","id":1016184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016170#post1016170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to whom does that Aura belong? Strictly speaking, yes, you Lash Out against Predatory Auras, not against vampires. But the difference is pretty academic. Point is, it's not Awe that you Lash Out at, it's the Deva's Aura, which has been altered by the effect of Awe.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's correct. I should have said it ends <i>for you</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The results we are speaking of are entirely the same. and I do see your point. I picture it as more of... You know in the movies the one guy is shooting fire from his hands and the other is ice, then there is this whole mess of fire and ice in the middle? You're two powers are pushing at the other and there is this battle to see which power is stronger. Say the ice gets through and breaks a hole in the fire, but the fire just splits down the sides, but it's still there. Like the vampire is still there, but your power was just stronger. Your power has put you in a protective bubble against theirs. not that the vampire can't hurt you, but that power just cant get through your metaphysical shield you put up.<br /> Or the vampire is attacking you with a car and you hit the car to stop the vampire. The vampire is the owner of the car, but you are just attacking that instead... Either way the vampire and the car aren't hurting you.<br /> <br /> Though that is just a purely an imaginative difference. Either way the lashing out is stopping the power from hurting you. As we all know, I tend to take the more literal take on the words in the book, but there is nothing wrong with saying you are lashing at the vampire.<br /> <br /> I suppose I have read to much Anita Blake and Vampire Chronicles where powers are more metaphysically tangible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T07:53:36-08:00","id":1016549,"title":"","content":"On the lashing out against effects, I rule similar to Vitalis.<br /> <br /> I also don't have the loser suffer a condition for losing this kind of contest.<br /> <br /> I don't see any reason why you shouldn't be able to lash out against effects. But I'll go re read that part before commenting further.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T09:07:41-08:00","id":1016584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016549#post1016549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any reason why you shouldn't be able to lash out against effects. But I'll go re read that part before commenting further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me put it this way. If you Lash Out against Awe, who rolls Power Attribute + Blood Potency?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T09:13:09-08:00","id":1016589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016584#post1016584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me put it this way. If you Lash Out against Awe, who rolls Power Attribute + Blood Potency?</div> </div> </div> </div>The player of the character that activated Awe.<br /> The ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T09:38:18-08:00","id":1016604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016584#post1016584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me put it this way. If you Lash Out against Awe, who rolls Power Attribute + Blood Potency?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Tsusasi, both the vampires roll their Power stat+ BP. Though instead of the vampire being affected, the power is affected with the result.<br /> Again I reiterate, the book literally says you attack the power. If you win the lashing out rolls as per page 92, the power stops working on you, Not the vampire is affected by the conditions, but the power stops working on you.<br /> <br /> Say the aura is a car, and the vampire is the driver. You can smash (lashing out) up the car to stop the vampire, The vampire rolls his drive to control the car, but once the car is stopped, the vampire is still ok and able to do what he needs to do.<br /> The car doesnt roll it's own drive.. same with the aura, the vampire rolls for both. It's a test of power and control.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It's not a huge deal to play it either way. Whatever works, the results are exactly the same. The power is stopped or not stopped. It's just how you want to picture it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 12-13-2016, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T09:43:39-08:00","id":1016606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016589#post1016589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The player of the character that activated Awe.<br /> The ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, and who's Power Attribute + Blood Potency are the player/ST rolling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T09:55:19-08:00","id":1016612,"title":"","content":"Using the stats of the character that's using the Awe effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T10:04:09-08:00","id":1016616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016612#post1016612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using the stats of the character that's using the Awe effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. So then who's Predatory Aura is it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T13:16:54-08:00","id":1016704,"title":"","content":"Lashing Out is basically a contest of wills between Beasts. It's vying for dominance. The power stops because your Beast has proven itself dominant to the other Vampire's Beast. Awe is a modified Predatory Aura. This has been confirmed elsewhere in the forums. When someone Lashes Out at you, you don't counter by Lashing Out at their Predatory Aura. You counter by Lashing Out at them directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T14:29:29-08:00","id":1016738,"title":"","content":"I really wish Lashing Out was just a common way to break mental effects. I feel like doing that instead of having specific disciplines be broken via lashing out would clear up a lot pf confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T19:05:55-08:00","id":1016863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016738#post1016738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really wish Lashing Out was just a common way to break mental effects. I feel like doing that instead of having specific disciplines be broken via lashing out would clear up a lot pf confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It wouldnt be fair to Nightmare, Majesty and Dominate users to have something that everyone can just end whenever they feel like when you cant stop Protean and Auspex","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T19:05:55-08:00","id":1016864,"title":"","content":"Ummm.... I have no idea why that posted 4 times ... So sorry. If i could delete it.. I would<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 12-13-2016, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T23:23:44-08:00","id":1016927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016738#post1016738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really wish Lashing Out was just a common way to break mental effects. I feel like doing that instead of having specific disciplines be broken via lashing out would clear up a lot pf confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It appears to be a common way to break effects that <i>modify the user's Predatory Aura</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T01:14:15-08:00","id":1016941,"title":"","content":"So, does anyone have a cheat-list with the powers you get to lash out at?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T02:04:29-08:00","id":1016954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016704#post1016704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lashing Out is basically a contest of wills between Beasts. It's vying for dominance. The power stops because your Beast has proven itself dominant to the other Vampire's Beast. Awe is a modified Predatory Aura. This has been confirmed elsewhere in the forums. When someone Lashes Out at you, you don't counter by Lashing Out at their Predatory Aura. You counter by Lashing Out at them directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet you can lash out at things that do not have Beasts, so it is not simply that. It is an intensification of the Predatory Aura, that may or may not trigger a direct clash with another vampire's Predatory Aura, another supernatural's &quot;some sort&quot; of aura, or even a mortal's strength of will. Or in this case simply shake off a supernatural effect by letting that aspect of herself a little loose.<br /> <br /> So while I understand how people can choose to interpret it the way you do, it is not a clear cut or set in stone interpretation.<br /> <br /> I haven't found anything to suggest it is in fact even a more sensible interpretation than mine (or Vitali's), so I won't be changing that (sans a new argument that actually does change my mind <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T03:37:21-08:00","id":1016972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016941#post1016941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, does anyone have a cheat-list with the powers you get to lash out at?</div> </div> </div> </div>From my observations, lashing out can only potentially end powers that adversely affect victims that are mechanically denied resist checks and don't require a roll to activate. Auspex is the only explicitly noteworthy exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T05:45:31-08:00","id":1017006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016941#post1016941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, does anyone have a cheat-list with the powers you get to lash out at?</div> </div> </div> </div> All of Majesty. <br /> <br /> Nightmare 1. <br /> <br /> Obfuscate 3 (and once Cloak of Night is shattered, all uses of Obfuscate are simultaneously shattered).<br /> <br /> You can Lash Out against powers that rely on Predator's Auras that you can see / identify. Majesty, Nightmare and Obfuscate are all powers that can be Lashed Out against from this criteria. Obfuscate 3 is only lashed out against once Auspex spots them. Nightmare powers can be used either subtly (and thus unidentified) or obviously (which involves using Nightmare 1) for more power. And Nightmare 1 can be Lashed Out against, ending the ability. <br /> <br /> In theory, you could Lash Out against Dominate to break it, as that also uses Aura, but every Dominate power makes you passive, and Lashing Out is definietly an agressive move. So, its not quite a valid method in the majority of cases. I suppose you could test it out by ordering the vampire to lash out against your control, but that is a bit of a niche case, unlikely to come up outside of an Ordo experiement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T14:35:38-08:00","id":1017319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1017006#post1017006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> All of Majesty.<br /> <br /> Nightmare 1.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate 3 (and once Cloak of Night is shattered, all uses of Obfuscate are simultaneously shattered).<br /> <br /> You can Lash Out against powers that rely on Predator's Auras that you can see / identify. Majesty, Nightmare and Obfuscate are all powers that can be Lashed Out against from this criteria. Obfuscate 3 is only lashed out against once Auspex spots them. Nightmare powers can be used either subtly (and thus unidentified) or obviously (which involves using Nightmare 1) for more power. And Nightmare 1 can be Lashed Out against, ending the ability.<br /> <br /> In theory, you could Lash Out against Dominate to break it, as that also uses Aura, but every Dominate power makes you passive, and Lashing Out is definietly an agressive move. So, its not quite a valid method in the majority of cases. I suppose you could test it out by ordering the vampire to lash out against your control, but that is a bit of a niche case, unlikely to come up outside of an Ordo experiement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait wait wait. So if I am charmed, I can lash out and be uncharmed? Or even...cancel Enthrall? if they have twisted my feelings with Majesty 3, I can lash out and Untwist them?<br /> Or if I am dominated, I can lash out and be not dominated? Say Bob gets dominated, Joe thinks his friend Bob is acting weird so he lashes out and cancels the dominate?<br /> Protean is a predatory aura too, it's just a physical manifestation of it, So are you saying that I can lash out against that and they need to shift back? They said in some thread that all disciplines are just their beast manifesting in someway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1016972#post1016972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From my observations, lashing out can only potentially end powers that adversely affect victims that are mechanically denied resist checks and don't require a roll to activate. Auspex is the only explicitly noteworthy exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed: <br /> <br /> As far as I know AS WRITTEN it only says Majesty 1, Nightmare 1 and Obfuscate 3. Obfuscate 3 is the only one that stops working where as Majesty 1 and nightmare 1 still work, they dont cancel, but you are simply not affected by them any longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T15:11:10-08:00","id":1017341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1017319#post1017319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait wait wait. So if I am charmed, I can lash out and be uncharmed? Or even...cancel Enthrall? if they have twisted my feelings with Majesty 3, I can lash out and Untwist them?<br /> Or if I am dominated, I can lash out and be not dominated? Say Bob gets dominated, Joe thinks his friend Bob is acting weird so he lashes out and cancels the dominate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure no to all of the above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1017319#post1017319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Protean is a predatory aura too, it's just a physical manifestation of it, So are you saying that I can lash out against that and they need to shift back? They said in some thread that all disciplines are just their beast manifesting in someway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Protean is a physical manifestation of the Beast, but it doesn't modify the user's Predatory Aura.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016077-majesty-5-idol-discipline?p=1017319#post1017319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed: <br /> <br /> As far as I know AS WRITTEN it only says Majesty 1, Nightmare 1 and Obfuscate 3. Obfuscate 3 is the only one that stops working where as Majesty 1 and nightmare 1 still work, they dont cancel, but you are simply not affected by them any longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is correct. I would also argue that those are the only Discipline powers in the core book that modify the user's Predatory Aura. Though, an argument could probably be made that Obfuscate 1 does as well.<br /> <br /> I think what MCN was getting at regarding Majesty is that all of its abilities above 1 rely on 1 to work. So, if you Lash Out to make yourself immune to a Daeva's Awe, they can't affect you with Confidant because Confidant requires the subject to be under the effects of Awe. They can't affect you with Loyalty because Loyalty requires the subject to have the Charmed Condition, which as established above, you can't inflict on someone unless they're under the effects of Awe. They can't affect you with Green Eyes because it requires the subject to have the Charmed or Enthralled Condition, which again, you can only inflict on someone affected by Awe. If they activate Idol, it won't affect you because Idol enhances the effects of Awe. You can't Lash Out to end a Charmed or Enthralled Condition once it's on you, because those are Conditions that affect <i>you</i>, not the Predatory Aura of the vampire using them. But, since they all rely on the victims being Awed by the user's Predatory Aura, you can avoid getting them in the first place by Lashing Out to prevent the user's Aura from Aweing you.<br /> <br /> Nightmare, on the other hand, does not require the victim to be affected by Dread Presence to work. Dread Presence does enhance all of the higher effects of Nightmare in some way, but unlike Majesty, they all at least do [i]something[i] to victims who are not affected by Dread Presence. So, Lashing Out to make yourself immune to Dread Presence can shield you from the worst effects of Nightmare, but it won't save you completely.<br /> <br /> All of Dominate's abilities rely on placing Conditions on the victim, and none of them modify the user's Aura, so Lashing Out doesn't protect you from it at all.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate is a little odd, because Face in the Crowd does affect the user's Predatory Aura, but it does so by suppressing it rather than weaponizing it. Presumably it can't be Lashed Out against because it explicitly makes the vampire's Predatory Aura disappear, and you can't Lash Out at an Aura you can't perceive. Cloak of Night, on the other hand, explicitly does allow vampires who can perceive the user to sense her Predatory Aura, therefore it can be Lashed Out at, and doing so ends the effects of Cloak of Night. To me this implies that Cloak of Night works a little differently, using the Predatory Aura to distort the senses of those who would perceive the user, as opposed to Familiar Stranger which conceals the Aura so that people overlook the user.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}